OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-$-%%%-!-%%%" ,%-$ -$%%-% ,,
OL,3,GNEWSAD-Day veteran who survived capture
OL,4,Adies aged 101
OL,5,
OL,6,FNormandy veteran Kenneth Hay, who
OL,7,Fsurvived being captured just weeks
OL,8,Fafter D-Day and spent years educating
OL,9,Fchildren about World War Two, has died
OL,10,Faged 101.
OL,12,FHay, from Upminster in east London,
OL,13,Fserved in the 4th Dorset Infantry
OL,14,FRegiment. He was captured a month after
OL,15,Fthe allied invasion of northern France
OL,16,Fand survived a 1,000-mile (1,609km)
OL,17,Fforced march in eastern Europe until he
OL,18,Fwas liberated by US forces.
OL,20,FHis death was announced on Sunday by
OL,21,Fthe British Normandy Memorial, for
OL,22,Fwhich he was an ambassador.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
